module bindings.go.backupstorage_reads;

// vitess's backupstorage package documents BackupHandle as the handle on an
// individual backup and its ReadFile as "starts reading a file from a
// backup", over whichever BackupStorage implementation the operator pointed
// the deployment at (a GCS or S3 bucket, or a plain directory). A file read
// back out of that store is data some other writer put there -- whoever
// took the backup, or anyone with write access to the bucket -- not a value
// this process computed, so the read is a code.StoredDataRead source, the
// same treatment redis reads, object stores and PHP session reads already
// get. The restore path JSON-decodes the MANIFEST it fetches this way and
// acts on the decoded fields, so a label here is what lets a stored field's
// journey into a sink be traced; whether any particular use of a decoded
// field is a problem stays the rules' call.
binding backupHandleReadFileStoredData {
  query pattern callExpr where callee.method == "ReadFile" and callee.receiver.type == "backupstorage.BackupHandle"
  emit source code.StoredDataRead at call.result
}
